<!-- _search_hiddenfield.erb
     A HiddenField (see _hiddenfield.erb) is invisible on the add/edit form
     - the user never sees or picks it, it's populated by local:has-defaults
     (e.g. project_category, defaulted per-form to distinguish Research vs
     Personnel Project records). But it's still a genuine controlled-
     vocabulary field with a real answer-block, and searching/filtering
     records BY that value (e.g. "show me all Personnel Project records")
     is exactly the kind of thing a search form should support - so unlike
     add/edit mode, search mode renders it as an ordinary dropdown, same
     shape as _search_radio.erb, rather than hiding it. -->
<div class="inputtype">
  <select name="<%= @question.questionid %>" id="<%= @answerblock.ablockid %>" width="70">
    <option value="">-- select an option --</option>
    <% @answerblock.answers.each do |answer| %>
      <% selected = (@thisval == answer.answer || @thisval == answer.answerid) ? "selected" : "" %>
      <option value="<%= answer.answerid %>" <%= selected %>><%= answer.answer %></option>
    <% end %>
  </select>
</div>
